meta {
  name: Delete Connection (DESTRUCTIVE)
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

delete {
  url: {{snaptradeBaseUrl}}/authorizations/{{snaptradeConnectionId}}?userId={{snaptradeUserId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  # Destructive — read before running

  Revokes a brokerage connection at SnapTrade. **This cannot be undone.**

  After this, every account under that connection stops returning data, and
  restoring it means re-linking through the Connection Portal in a browser and
  waiting for the initial holdings and transaction syncs again — the
  transaction backfill is the slow part.

  Set `snaptradeConnectionId` deliberately from **List Connections**; do not
  rely on a leftover value. There is no assert and no post-response var here on
  purpose, so this request does nothing useful by accident and is never part of
  a folder run.

  It is included because exposing connection removal to end users is required
  by SnapTrade's launch checklist, so the endpoint needs to be exercised at
  least once — ideally against a throwaway connection rather than your real
  Vanguard link.
}
